<div class="field field--name--field-text-with-media field--type--text-long field--label--hidden">
    
      <div  class="field-text-with-media">  <div class="tex2jax_process"><p>Aftershocks are a sequence of earthquakes that happen after a larger mainshock on a fault. Aftershocks occur near the fault zone where the mainshock rupture occurred and are part of the "readjustment process” after the main slip on the fault. Aftershocks become less frequent with time, although they can continue for days, weeks, months, or even years for a very large mainshock. A swarm, on the...</p></div>

